{title: Careless Love}
{artist: Traditional American}
{key: C}
{tempo: 92}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, blues, ballad}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Love, oh love, oh [G7]careless [C]love [C]
[C]Love, oh love, oh [C7]careless [F]love [F]
[F]Love, oh love, oh [F]careless [C]love [C]
You [C]see what [G7]careless love has [C]done [C]

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]When I wore my [G7]apron [C]low [C]
[C]You'd follow me [C7]through rain and [F]snow [F]
[F]Now I wear my [F]apron [C]high [C]
You [C]see my [G7]door and you pass it [C]by [C]

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]I love my mama and [G7]papa [C]too [C]
[C]I love my mama and [C7]papa [F]too [F]
[F]I love my mama and [F]papa [C]too [C]
But I'd [C]leave them [G7]both to go with [C]you [C]
